# The reference corpus is stored byte-for-byte. It is read-only material that is
# never edited in-repo, and it contains UTF-16 tree listings that end-of-line
# conversion would corrupt.
docs-ref/** -text

# Generated data. Diffing them is noise and normalising them would rewrite files
# the tool reads back verbatim.
#
# These paths said `src/data/reference/` until 2026-09-02. That was v1's layout;
# v2 moved the engine to `engine/` and the rules quietly stopped matching
# anything, so the files they were written to protect were unprotected for the
# whole of v2. Measured before fixing: no damage done -- the blobs and the
# working tree are byte-identical -- but the guard was off.
engine/data/reference/*.json -text -diff
engine/data/reference/*.xlsx binary
